{
 "_doc": "Vharlen's own travellers and folk (Expansion 1), laid over data/provinces/travellers.json key by key (js/sim/province-files.js): `kinds`, `folk` and `fighters` are the island's; `rules` is the home file's. Same shapes as the home file (read its _doc). Kinds walk data/provinces/vharlen-routes.json; display names use data/names/vharlen.json. Folk `props` use only data/vignettes/vharlen-props.json ids (tests/W/vharlen-dressing.test.js). Chatter pools are the island ones in data/names/chatter.json (`role.<island role>`, `road.isle_*`). Beasts are `none` or `mule` (no oxen, horses or cattle on the island). Nobody here herds anything.",
 "fighters": {
  "_doc": "Report #18 (wrap-up 2026-10-13): who in the wilds FIGHTS the monsters beside them while a player is near (js/rules/guards.js 'wanderer': nothing happens with nobody watching; they never die, they sit down and get up again; helping one earns thanks by economy.json npcThanks). `roles` = a placed NPC, a set-piece or wayside worker, a fort's garrison or a village's own guard with one of these roles fights (js/sim/realm.js marks the placed ones, js/sim/travellers.js the wayside ones). `crew` 'armed' = a traveller on the road fights when its crew row says `armed: true` (caravan guards, road patrols, a collector's escort, hunting parties). Everyone else — traders, farmers, pilgrims, children, shepherds — stays out of it. Each fights at the level of the zone it stands in (the floor of its band + `levelOver`). Vharlen: the island's own fighting roles (hired spears, Council wardens, Rim Keepers, salamander trappers, eel spearers); guard / sergeant / captain stay for the town guards and fort garrisons.",
